    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Tourism</span> is the activity of travelling to and staying in places outside one's usual environment for leisure, business, cultural or other purposes, and it represents a significant economic sector for many countries.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning and Importance of Tourism</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Tourism involves temporary travel away from home for recreation, culture, business or other purposes. It is important because it generates income, creates employment, earns foreign exchange, and promotes cultural exchange and international understanding.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Types of Tourism</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Domestic tourism</td><td>Travel within one's own country</td></tr><tr><td>International tourism</td><td>Travel to a foreign country</td></tr><tr><td>Eco-tourism</td><td>Travel focused on experiencing and conserving natural environments</td></tr><tr><td>Cultural tourism</td><td>Travel focused on experiencing a region's history, traditions, arts and heritage</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Tourist Attractions in Nigeria and West Africa</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Attraction</th><th>Location / Significance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Yankari Game Reserve</td><td>Bauchi State, Nigeria — wildlife and warm springs</td></tr><tr><td>Obudu Mountain Resort</td><td>Cross River State, Nigeria — scenic highland resort</td></tr><tr><td>Osun-Osogbo Sacred Grove</td><td>Osun State, Nigeria — UNESCO World Heritage cultural site</td></tr><tr><td>Olumo Rock</td><td>Abeokuta, Ogun State, Nigeria — historic rock formation</td></tr><tr><td>Cape Coast Castle</td><td>Ghana — historic site linked to the transatlantic slave trade</td></tr><tr><td>Lake Volta</td><td>Ghana — one of the largest man-made lakes in the world</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Benefits of Tourism</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Generates employment in hospitality, transport and related services.</li><li>Earns valuable foreign exchange from international visitors.</li><li>Supports infrastructure development (roads, airports, hotels).</li><li>Promotes preservation of natural and cultural heritage.</li><li>Encourages cross-cultural understanding and goodwill.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Challenges of Tourism</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Insecurity and negative perception discouraging visitors.</li><li>Inadequate infrastructure and poor maintenance of tourist sites.</li><li>Insufficient marketing and promotion of attractions internationally.</li><li>Environmental degradation from poorly managed tourist activity.</li><li>Seasonal fluctuations affecting income stability in the sector.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be able to name at least two specific Nigerian tourist attractions, as site-specific examples are commonly required.</div>",
